      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779769544215,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Now your service can depend on the\ninterface shape.\n- Clean mental model\n    -> Service \n        -> Repo Interface\n            -> Repo Implementation\n                -> ORM Model\n                    -> Database\n\nThe model is usually the most directly\ncoupled to the ORM schema.\n\nThe repository implementation is also coupled\nbecause it calls ORM/model methods.\n\nBut the repository contract/interface can be\nindependent, and that is what your service\nshould ideally depend on in a very clean\narchitecture.",
      "fontSize": 13.815700128739836,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "Y6t3VJN4A3MpPmv5ByjGW",
      "originalText": "- Now your service can depend on the interface shape.\n- Clean mental model\n    -> Service \n        -> Repo Interface\n            -> Repo Implementation\n                -> ORM Model\n                    -> Database\n\nThe model is usually the most directly coupled to the ORM schema.\n\nThe repository implementation is also coupled because it calls ORM/model methods.\n\nBut the repository contract/interface can be independent, and that is what your service should ideally depend on in a very clean architecture.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
